Subject: [PATCH] slice-ws2812: fix DMA FIFO address on Compute Module 3

Commit 487abec ("Fix DMA bus address for Compute Module 3 - add
BCM2835_VCMMU_SHIFT offset") tried to fix the WS2812 LEDs on CM3 by
adding BCM2835_VCMMU_SHIFT to the PWM FIFO bus address returned from
the device tree "reg" property. In practice this produces a DMA FIFO
address the DMA engine cannot actually reach on CM3 (BCM2837), and the
LEDs stay dark even though DMA submissions succeed without error.

Verified on hardware (webcam brightness measurement, on/off/color
sweep) that the DMA engine on CM3 requires the ARM *physical* address
of the PWM peripheral (0x3fxxxxxx), not the VideoCore bus address
(0x7exxxxxx) with an extra VCMMU shift applied on top of it. Compute
the correct physical FIFO address directly instead.

diff --git a/ws2812.c b/ws2812.c
--- a/ws2812.c
+++ b/ws2812.c
@@ -94,7 +94,10 @@ struct ws2812_state {
  #define BCM2708_PERI_BASE 0x20000000
 #endif
 
-#define BCM2835_VCMMU_SHIFT		(0x7E000000 - BCM2708_PERI_BASE)
+/* CM3 (BCM2837) ARM physical peripheral base; DMA needs the physical
+ * address here, not the VideoCore bus address used elsewhere. */
+#define CM3_PERI_PHYS_BASE		0x3f000000
+#define BCM2835_BUS_BASE		0x7e000000
 
 /* Each LED is controlled with a 24 bit RGB value
  * each bit is created from a nibble of data either
@@ -467,7 +470,8 @@ static int ws2812_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	/* request a DMA channel */
-	cfg.dst_addr = state->phys_addr + PWM_FIFO1 + BCM2835_VCMMU_SHIFT;
+	cfg.dst_addr = state->phys_addr - BCM2835_BUS_BASE +
+		       CM3_PERI_PHYS_BASE + PWM_FIFO1;
 	ret = dmaengine_slave_config(state->dma_chan, &cfg);
 	if (ret < 0)
 	{
